            "review_title": "Review at Quán Bự - Cây Bàng",
            "review_text": "aubsters\nSan Diego52 contributions\n0\nAn Amazing First Meal in Hanoi\nApr 2017 • Friends\nI kind of don't want to tell you all about this gem my friend and I found, but...I believe that it's important for us travelers to share experiences so here you go. We asked our hotel staff where we should go for dinner and they suggested anywhere on Hang Buom Street. We were exploring the weekend (pedestrian only) night market and found our street. We stopped at one place for a $3 Magner Cider (I'm used to paying $10) and continued our journey when this short Asian woman practically tackled us to come to her sidewalk street food \"restaurant.\" We looked at the place which was PACKED with locals (that's the key here...if the locals are there, its good and cheap). We ordered the meat mix grill which came with a bottle of oil, carton of butter, a grill, and heaping amounts of meat, herbs, veggies, and french baguette. Not really knowing what we were doing, a local next to us showed us what we needed to do and....what an amazing meal. This, plus 4 beers came to 280K VND (or @ $12 USD). Seriously, check this place out AND this street. Come on a Friday or Saturday night and prepare to party. And keep in mind, THIS IS street food...there is no luxury here.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 20, 2017",
